# Always return a PR summary after creating a pull request

Ported from `.claude/rules/pr-summaries.md`. Creating a PR is a visible, shared-state action —
getting confirmation to open it is not the same as telling the user what actually shipped. On a
project with contributors on both Claude Code and Cursor working async
(`parallel-work-boundaries.mdc`), the PR description isn't guaranteed to be read the moment it's
created.

## The rule

Whenever a pull request is created in this repo, follow it with a written summary in the chat
response, not just the PR URL. Include:

- The PR title and URL.
- What changed, in plain language — not a copy of the diff.
- Anything the requester should act on before merge: an incomplete test-plan item, an open
  question the PR doesn't resolve, or a follow-up it depends on.

A bare "PR created: `<url>`" does not satisfy this rule.
